# The production picker opened for a line of the base's queue (a click on the queue's first line): the buttons at the foot are HELP, OK,
# REPLACE, INSERT, DELETE and CANCEL, and the costs are counted without what the base has already made. Insert puts the marked
# choice into the queue, Replace changes the line's, Delete takes it out, and Cancel leaves it; the base (its queue) is part of
# the state compared. See prodpicker.scene for the rest. Leave time after each step; the snaps take 2 s each.
# The leaders' portraits in the base screen animate on their own slow clock.
mask 266 625 310 678
mask 702 624 760 680
mask 318 98 708 295      # the map of the base screen, whose terrain can come out in two looks
25 load
48 click 362 734         # the note's Close
55 key b                 # found a base where the colony pod stands
64 key Return            # its base screen
68 state pp_sel 0x6b27b8 12
68 state pp_mode 0x6a8ba8 16
72 click 190 605         # the first line of the queue
76 move 600 420
80 snap open
82 click 510 120         # Network Node
86 snap marked
88 click 561 515         # INSERT
96 snap inserted
98 click 190 605         # the first line again, now holding it
104 snap open-filled
106 click 377 120        # Colony Pod
110 snap marked-again
112 click 459 515        # REPLACE
120 snap replaced
122 click 190 605
128 snap open-replaced
130 click 664 515        # DELETE
138 snap deleted
140 click 190 605
146 snap open-empty
148 click 767 515        # CANCEL
154 snap cancelled
156 close
